    "result_text": "All 56 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: an optional `title` (e.g. MR/MRS/MS/DR) on owner creation, with the response exposing a derived `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is supplied.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `salutation` (read-only, derived) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) are generated from this spec at build.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter so the value persists and survives the create\u2192re-read cycle.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation(owner)` helper mapped onto `OwnerDto.salutation`, following the existing derived-field convention (a blank title is treated as absent). The `title` input flows onto the entity automatically via the existing `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` MapStruct mapping.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table in every schema (tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the SQL is authoritative).\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests.coreComposesSalutation` passes (`DR` + `who` \u2192 `\"DR who\"`), and the full suite (56 tests) is green.",
